WEBVTT

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.790
Black Knight Onyx,

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.920
I hereby decree that your temporary status is to be lifted,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.630
and you are to become the fifth member
of the Great Generals from this day forth.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.580
Signed, Demon Queen Echidna.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.880
He is a newcomer, yes, but
a steadfast supporter of our cause.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:30.250
And I can think of no man better suited
to extend a hand to humanity on our behalf.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.880
With him our quest for the Philosopher's Stone may no
longer be futile.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.920
Adding a fifth to our Four Great Generals
may pose some problems,

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.880
but I will discuss that with the others.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.630
I know I've made the right choice with him.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.710
Dire news, Your Highness!
The Great Spirit Portal is closing up!

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.170
Do we know why?

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.920
No, but we've begun to run low on
the rare crystal catalysts that keep it open!

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.000
I'll help!

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.040
Never did I think it would come to this...

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.170
Not at the very moment where
our future seemed secured.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.420
Live, live on, with all your might

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.880
Follow the light to the future

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:36.750
Betrayed and left behind in this lonely world

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.290
Fearing a tomorrow I've lost sight of

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.460
I search for the place I belong

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:51.960
My heart screams out, "I want to be needed"

00:01:53.170 --> 00:02:00.710
I want to puzzle out these entwined identities, but can I trust them?

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.080
Live, live on, with all your might

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.080
Follow the light to the future

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.580
Even if you lose everything

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.920
Stay connected to hope

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.630
I don't know why I'm here

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.500
But that's all right with me right now

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.420
I have to overcome and press on

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.330
So I can smile with you again

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.630
This is a crisis situation.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:52.000
Thanks to Shutina, Lord Onyx, and myself,
the Portal is stable--but only for now.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.380
In its current state, it won't last longer
than seven days, perhaps less.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.210
Indeed.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.960
Lily, save the cookies for later.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.380
That doesn't mean you should switch to an apple!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.380
Hey, Echidna, what'll happen if
the Big Spirit Thingy closes up?

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.250
We won't be able to return to the Demon World.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:09.960
Huh?!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.920
Once it closes,

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.080
we've no idea how long it will be before
another is opened to bring troops through.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.580
It could be centuries, or millennia...

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.210
All more time during which the Demon World suffers.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.250
We must decide upon our army's next plans
within these next seven days.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.920
Shutina, what is your opinion?

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.250
I believe we have two choices.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.790
We could return to the Demon World
before the Portal closes.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.380
Retreat, then.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.250
Our current army consists mostly
of denizens of the human realm.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:49.580
Since we cannot bring them with us,
we will need to disband our army.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.290
Which means we'd have to go our separate ways, too.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.290
I don't want us to break up!
Not when we've all become such good friends!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.830
So retreat's Option 1. What's Option 2?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:05.080
The second option is to immediately
mobilize our army, attack Renailles,

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.920
and take the Philosopher's Stone for ourselves.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.250
That seems out of the question.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.290
I would say so.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.540
As would I.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.670
Our current forces are far weaker than
they were during our last campaign.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.330
Bringing them into battle would
cause only foolhardy bloodshed,

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.460
especially knowing the humans still have their
greatest ally:

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.380
Leo Demonhart!

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.460
If only we were rid of him...

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.000
Lord Onyx. Have you ever fought the Hero Leo?

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.540
No, but I've heard stories.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:41.080
I fought against him, one on one,
with all of my might, and still I was defeated.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.460
So this I can say with confidence:

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.080
He is a monster, a force to be reckoned with.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:49.920
If we engaged him as we are,
he would wipe out every last one of our troops.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.130
Obtaining the Philosopher's Stone would
be the least of our concerns.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:58.040
I do not fear death. I left the Demon World
knowing I may die here.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.750
But I am not willing to lead others to that same fate.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:07.960
My decision is made.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.830
The army is to be disbanded,
and we will return to the Demon World.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:17.040
Shutina and I must return. I am the
Demon World's leader, and she is my second.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:23.750
Returning without the Philosopher's Stone
will inevitably lead to conflict over the throne.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:29.960
They all seem at a loss for words. I understand.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:34.380
Hey, Echidna, I know you're worried
about him, but he's actually--

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.750
We should just tell her.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:37.920
N-no, we shouldn't!

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.540
It's fine, I know. You needn't say anything, Shutina.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.880
We may be 300 years apart in age,
but we've known each other for a long time.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:54.210
You know more than anyone the faith and
hope I've put into the quest for the Stone.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.630
Now's not the time, Lily!

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.750
I know this decision weighs heavily upon you.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.000
It's nothing of importance!

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.040
Thank you all for staying by my side.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:15.710
As the ruler of the Demon World--no,
as the solitary demon Echidna, I thank you.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:23.000
No, this is unseemly of me! A Queen should
not show her subjects this much weakness!

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.380
I must remain proud till the bitter end!

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:31.000
We will need to start over to find
a new method of saving our Demon World.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:38.130
You want to better the lives of your people.
You told me this when we drank together, yes?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.670
Yes. One cannot maintain order in a barren wasteland.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:48.420
I would use the stone to bring about warm sun,
lush greenery, clean air and water,

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.710
the same with which the human world is blessed.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.960
Since I was young, I've studied and trained for that plan,

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:59.040
all to become the Demon Queen
and travel to the human world.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:04.420
I held fast to those hopes and dreams,
knowing the Stone would grant my desires.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:10.250
Yet now, it all ends in defeat.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.170
First, let me make one thing clear.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:18.250
The Stone is not an all-powerful wish-granting device.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:23.210
It is an advanced engine from the Mechanical Age that
utilizes a micro black hole

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.540
to produce nigh-unlimited energy.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.790
I cannot be sure it would grant your desires.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.250
I see.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:36.710
I'd imagine a detailed manual on its operation
is hiding somewhere in the human world.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:43.380
Humans are looking for it too,
but its antiquity has made it rather tough to find.

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:48.920
All the more reason for us
to seek peace with the humans.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.880
If we worked together to find
this 'manual' of which you speak...

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.960
No, that would be pointless.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:02.130
We would have to steal the Stone from them.
Our peace would end in war.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.500
In any case, it's far too late for us to consider this path.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.580
You needn't worry about that.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.960
As far as I know, there are two
Philosopher's Stones in the human world.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.420
Two?!

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:20.960
Yes. You only need one to accomplish
your mission, correct?

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.540
That leaves one for the human world
and one for the Demon World.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:27.460
Two Stones... Could it be?

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.380
Would that not be ideal for creating peace
between your two realms?

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.710
And could you cut the crap and look at me?

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.710
Where's Lord Onyx?

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.170
Echidna, keep turning!

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.170
The situation's too dire, so I ditched my disguise.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.210
Listen closely, Echidna.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.880
Wh... Wha...

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:57.330
First, I'm sorry I had to trick you,
but it was the only way.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:00.960
Here's the real reason I joined your army:

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:07.000
I wanted to see if you were truly worthy
of the Philosopher Stone's power.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:11.250
If I'd realized you weren't,
I would have left right then and there,

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.000
but when we spoke over dinner and wine,
I was convinced you were worthy.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:20.880
What wine?! The last drink I had was
when I bared my soul to Lord Onyx...

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.500
Where is he?! Where has Lord Onyx gone off to?!

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:27.330
I know you have the ability
to bring order to the Demon World.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:33.580
And if peace in your world means demons
will stop bothering humanity,

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.080
then giving you the Stone will be more than worth it.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:40.080
Wait, is Leo Lord Onyx?
Has Lord Onyx been Leo this whole time?!

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.710
I see. So that was the game.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.170
I've been had.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:59.790
Echidna, I know you're still processing
all this, but we're low on time.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.540
I know where the other Stone is--
the one that isn't in Renailles.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:10.380
Die, bastard!

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.670
When I look back on that moment now,

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:20.750
back then, we were no more than
the Hero and the Demon Queen...

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:32.830
I'm cold!

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:38.040
And the Stone will really,
TRULY be where you're leading us?

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.580
Yes, really, truly.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.460
You aren't leading us into some terrible trap?

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.130
Could you be any more skeptical?!

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:49.380
Do you even realize how much
I've helped your Demon Army?!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:53.580
Oh, I'm WELL aware of how much you've 'helped' us,
you blathering imbecile!

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.460
Yeah, after I so nicely explained it all,
you ungrateful moron!

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.290
C'mon, Echidna. Don't you have any other moves?

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.080
This is the same thing you did
when I came for my interview.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.670
Shut up. Don't speak. Drop dead.

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.960
You knew this was the only way I could do this.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:17.000
I had to join up under a false name and
earn my way to an audience with you.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.250
You wouldn't have let me join otherwise, would you?

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:22.420
Never in a thousand THOUSAND years
would I ever let you join us!

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.710
Now go eat some poison mushrooms,
suffer for three days, then die a rotten death!

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.170
How did I never realize it was you?!

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:34.830
I know now there were countless instances
where I should have known it was you!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.710
Damn it all! I should have been more cautious!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:40.170
I'll bear this shame for the rest of my life!

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:41.670
Sorry.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.920
And what infuriates me most of
all is how you are right as rain,

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.580
mere SECONDS after I hit you point-blank with Inferno!

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.880
Echidna!

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:51.880
Leo's been of great service to the Demon Army!

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:56.830
Won't you allow him to join us?
I owe him a great deal.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:58.540
And y'know something?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:03.500
Leo gave me lots of advice and
helped make logistics so much easier!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.580
And you know what else?

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.710
He greatly reduced my overtime hours!

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:10.880
Also, Echidna, the dining hall could definitely pay
the staff a lot more.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.790
My daughter Julietta is deeply grateful to him, too!

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:18.670
It's awesome! When we all work together,
work gets done super fast!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.040
I beg of you, please, show him mercy!

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.500
Yeah, he's kind of an ass, but I don't see why not.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.830
All right! Enough, all of you!

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:34.790
I shall make an exception and pardon you
for your deception as Lord Onyx.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.000
Thank you.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:41.750
That aside, is there truly another
Philosopher's Stone outside of Renailles?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:42.750
There is.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:46.040
You can find it in the Seshat Mountains.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:49.000
The Seshat Mountains? That's extremely close to here!

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:53.170
Yeah, but it's protected by a pretty powerful
guardian. Shouldn't be a problem, though.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:58.170
If Leo is describing it as powerful,
then how fearsome must it be?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.080
This sounds too good to be true.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.710
We can do it if we all work together!

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:04.920
We will come with you.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:10.790
Very well. I would prefer not to be left alone with
this insolent fool, after all.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:15.210
Let us go, then, to the Seshat Mountains!

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:24.830
I'm cold! I'm so cold! I'm freezing!

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:23.830
Lily is from the much warmer South.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.460
Same with you, right, Edvard?

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:29.920
I'm fine. My scales will stave off the cold.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:33.580
Huh. So where is this Stone at?

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:38.460
Just a little further, at the peak of that mountain.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.750
I'm cold! I'm gonna freeze to death!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.630
Amun, morph, alleg, warm.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.830
I'm so warm now!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.500
Thanks, Shutina!

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:52.170
You're quite welcome. You'd do well
to study some magic yourself, Lily.

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:02.130
Stubborn fool. Why did you teleport
us partway? Why make us walk?!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.710
Why waste our precious time?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:06.290
I wanted time to talk with you.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.040
Talk? What is there left to discuss?

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:11.630
Passing the torch, what else?

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:15.790
The Philosopher's Stone's been my big project
for ages, and it's gonna be yours soon.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.250
Wouldn't it be a good idea to hear more
about it from the person you're replacing?

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:26.630
Very well, O Wise One. What wisdom do
you have to share about the Stone?

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:32.750
Like I said before, the Stone isn't
some magic item you can use to grant wishes.

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.250
You understand that, right?

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:36.500
Of course.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:41.580
I know that planting it in the ground wouldn't cause
green fields to sprout overnight,

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:46.540
turn water to wine, or anything fanciful like that.

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:48.040
That's exactly right.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:53.670
Once you get the Stone, make peace with
humanity and search for the manual.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:59.210
A copy of the Akashic Engine Usage Manual
should be hiding somewhere out there.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:02.170
Without it, you won't know how to use the Stone.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.580
Peace with humanity...

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.210
Can you do it?

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:17.290
To be completely frank, until a little while ago,
I didn't think it was possible.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.080
You understand, yes?

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:25.250
We couldn't have stolen their most precious treasure
then asked for peace and harmony.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:31.750
But after speaking with Onyx--well,
you--my opinion changed completely.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:35.250
I know the story is just that, a story, but--

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:36.540
It's not just a story.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.210
It really happened.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:42.420
So don't worry. I know humans
and demons can live in harmony.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:50.380
But getting to that point is going to cost
a lot of blood, sweat, and tears.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.250
How foolish of you to underestimate me, Hero.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:16:01.290
I am the Demon Queen Echidna,
the most powerful ruler my world has ever known!

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:06.080
Blood, sweat, or tears, one by one,
I will endure it all to bring peace to fruition!

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:11.130
That so? Glad to hear it. Makes me feel better.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:21.670
That tone... He sounds so sad.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:25.170
Well, I hope you can defeat
any mighty foe that stands in your way.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.830
Like me. Oh, wait...

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:28.920
Impudent swine!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:29.920
Ack, that's cold!

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.460
Echidna, you ass!

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.830
Be thankful that was all I unleashed upon you!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:36.500
Perhaps it was just my imagination.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:37.710
Payback time!

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:40.250
What?!

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.250
Gah! Dammit, that's no fair!

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:49.040
I was worried about them for a moment,
but I'm glad they're getting along so well.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.960
That means we can be the FIVE Great Generals!

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:55.460
Wait, if we all work together, we'll be as
strong as A HUNDRED Great Generals!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.500
As long as everything keeps working out...

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.710
Leo.

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:02.380
Huh?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.750
There's something I've been wondering about.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:08.250
Why do you know so much about
the Mechanical Civilization?

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:11.000
That was roughly three thousand years ago,

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:15.540
the same human civilization
that King Belial invaded, correct?

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.580
Were you a scholar before becoming a hero?

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:23.000
Not really. I was just born back then.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:26.040
I see, so you were born in the Mechanical Age.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.250
Wait... What?!

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:33.420
If that were true, then he'd be
over three thousand years old!

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:38.250
Did he use some form of magic to extend his lifespan?!

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:39.420
No...

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.830
Is this Hero even human?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:48.500
When Belial attacked, humanity created
living bioweapons called the Demonhart Series.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.170
I am the fifth in that series.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:53.210
My design placed emphasis on
hyper-reactive skill improvement.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.290
Hyper... What?

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:59.920
I copy any and all abilities my opponents use
against me to develop my skills ad infinitum.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.500
I am the result of three thousand years
of hard-won experience.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:06.130
And the DH Series weapons don't die from old age.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:10.460
We keep living on, and on, and on,
which for me, meant growing stronger.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.290
Here I thought you'd be more surprised.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.540
It makes sense.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:23.580
It means you possess the strength of
untold hundreds of thousands of soldiers.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.960
Yeah, that's about right.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:33.710
Had I known just how powerful you were,
I would have found another route to the Stone.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:36.670
But despite what happened,
we eventually found each other.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.080
Not so bad when you put it that way, yeah?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.170
Hmph.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:45.960
One can never understand destiny,
even fate as strange as this.

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.960
Fate where, after defeating me in combat,

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:52.420
the Hero inexplicably joins my army and
takes me right to the Philosopher's Stone.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:57.750
All of the other DH Series weapons died off.
I'm the only one left.

00:18:58.210 --> 00:19:03.000
So you've lost all your brothers
and sisters. My condolences.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.080
Thanks.

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:09.880
They've embedded one critical order
in our cores: "protect humanity".

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:13.080
Protecting humanity is my sole identity.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.290
For thousands of years,
I've fought to bring about peace.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:21.250
And when peace came, I've wished
for more danger, more war to come.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:24.540
Are you a fool?! What would be the point in that?

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:27.460
Do you not enjoy your hard-won peace?!

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:30.670
Yeah, you're right. I should enjoy it.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:36.830
My skill development functionality put my orders
and my feelings all out of whack.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.380
I'm starting to lose it.

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:46.710
Sometimes, I get to thinking.
Am I just holding humanity back?

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:54.790
Humanity can function without a hero.
Am I just doing this for myself?

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:58.080
Am I forcing myself onto humanity?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.290
I don't believe you are.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:05.500
Without you, the human world would
most certainly be under my control.

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:07.500
Sure, this time.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:10.080
But what about next time?

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:15.880
One day, humanity might be able
to take down a Demon Queen all on their own.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:19.250
When that day comes, I won't have
a place to belong anymore.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.170
I'm pretty sure I'm breaking down.

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:28.670
And when I'm too far gone, I'll bring chaos to the world,

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.250
just to give myself a reason to keep protecting it.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.290
I'll plunge the world into disaster, then pull it back out.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:42.210
I'll become nothing more than a machine
that saves the world, over and over.

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:45.000
I'd be worse than any Demon Army.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:51.130
Before that happens, you know what
needs to be done, right, Echidna?

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:53.000
Leo, what are you saying?

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.290
We made it!

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:02.380
What a splendid view. It's almost as if nature
is rewarding us for making it this far.

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:03.460
I concur.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:05.790
Where's the guardian?

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:08.750
You're right, there's no one here.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.210
There is no guardian.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.380
I have the Philosopher's Stone.

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:28.130
It's the heart of the Demonhart Series. An infinite
generator, the Akashic Engine.

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.880
That is the Philosopher's Stone you're after.

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:34.040
Hold on. You mean to say...

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:35.250
Kill me.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:40.000
If you want the Stone, then kill me and tear out my heart.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:47.080
'Tis I, former Hero Leo Demonhart!

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:52.330
I'm a skilled swordsman and have mastered all
arcane schools of magic, including black magic!

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:55.210
I've even defeated the Demon Queen Echidna
herself in single combat!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.420
I am ready and raring to fight for your cause!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:59.710
Though still but a temporary employee,

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:02.920
as of this moment, I announce
my resignation from the Demon Army

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:06.420
and reiterate my desire to
exterminate humanity once and for all!

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:11.920
And I'll say this now: you don't get to run away.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:17.330
If you try to run, I will descend from this peak
and kill every last human I find.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:20.380
I'll even destroy the texts that tell you
how to use the Philosopher's Stone!

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:21.830
What...

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:26.580
You told me you want to save
the Demon World, right, Echidna?

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:30.710
You said you'd endure blood, sweat, and tears...

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:34.960
to obtain the stone and bring peace to fruition.

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:37.670
Blood, sweat, and tears.

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.790
The time to prove your mettle is now!

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:46.880
If you want the Stone, if you want to save the world,

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:51.210
<b>I Want to Quit Heroing</b>

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:48.670
then stop me, here and now,

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.080
brave heroes!

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>I'll Save</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>the World,</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Even If</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>That Means</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Destroying It</b>
